@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Accessibility statement for Heat Network Technical Assurance Scheme (HNTAS)";
}

<div class="govuk-width-container">
    <div class="govuk-grid-row">
        <div class="govuk-grid-column-full">

            <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">
                Accessibility statement for Heat Network Technical Assurance Scheme (HNTAS)
            </h1>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                This accessibility statement applies to the Heat Network Technical Assurance Scheme digital service.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                This service is run by the Department for Energy Security and Net Zero (DESNZ). We want as many people as possible to be able to use it. For example, you should be able to:
            </p>

            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>change colours, contrast levels and fonts</li>
                <li>zoom in up to 300% without text spilling off the screen</li>
                <li>navigate most of the service using only a keyboard</li>
                <li>navigate most of the service using speech recognition software</li>
                <li>listen to most of the service using a screen reader (including JAWS, NVDA and VoiceOver)</li>
            </ul>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We have also made the content as simple as possible to understand.
            </p>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                How accessible this service is
            </h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                This service is <strong>partially compliant with WCAG 2.2 AA.</strong>
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We have identified a small number of issues through automated testing. These are outlined below with context and mitigation.
            </p>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Non-accessible content
            </h2>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">
                1. ARIA attributes (tooling discrepancy – no user impact)
            </h3>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                Some elements include ARIA attributes flagged as unsupported by automated tooling.
            </p>

            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>These patterns originate from the GOV.UK Design System (for example, radios with conditional reveal)</li>
                <li>Attributes are dynamically applied in line with GOV.UK implementation guidance</li>
                <li>The issue is only identified by Axe and is not reproduced through other tools or manual testing</li>
                <li>No accessibility impact has been observed (keyboard navigation, screen readers and interaction behaviour function as expected)</li>
            </ul>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                This represents a <strong>tooling inconsistency rather than a confirmed WCAG 2.2 failure</strong>,
                and is therefore classified as <strong>non-actionable at service level</strong>.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We continue to monitor GOV.UK Design System updates and will adopt any upstream changes where required.
            </p>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">
                2. Documents (PDFs and external content)
            </h3>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                Some documents accessible via the service (for example, technical guidance and supporting materials) may not fully meet accessibility standards.
            </p>

            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>These documents are <strong>owned and maintained externally</strong> (GOV.UK)</li>
                <li>HNTAS <strong>does not control the creation or ongoing maintenance</strong> of these files</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Feedback and contact information
            </h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                If you find accessibility issues not listed on this page or need information in a different format, contact:
            </p>

            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>
                    Email: <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:hntas_digital.support@energysecurity.gov.uk">hntas_digital.support@energysecurity.gov.uk</a>
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We aim to respond within 5 working days.
            </p>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Enforcement procedure
            </h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) is responsible for enforcing the accessibility regulations.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                If you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS).
            </p>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Technical information about this service
            </h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                DESNZ is committed to making this service accessible, in accordance with:
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) Accessibility Regulations 2018
            </p>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Compliance status
            </h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                This service is <strong>partially compliant with WCAG 2.2 AA</strong>, due to the items described above.
            </p>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                What we’re doing to improve accessibility
            </h2>

            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>Monitoring <strong>GOV.UK Design System updates</strong> for upstream fixes</li>
                <li>Working with <strong>external content owners</strong> to improve document accessibility</li>
                <li>Continuing <strong>regular accessibility testing (automated + manual)</strong></li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Preparation of this accessibility statement
            </h2>

            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>Prepared on: <strong>05 June 2026</strong></li>
                <li>Last reviewed: <strong>30 June 2026</strong></li>
                <li>Last tested: <strong>05 June 2026</strong></li>
                <li>Tested by: <strong>Zoonou (WCAG-EM methodology)</strong></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>